@startuml SandboxSteps
' SPEC source (the real orchestration this diagram tracks):
'   internal/run/run.go           — run.Do() host flow (requireSandbox … launchSandbox)
'   internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go — Kit, sbx secret store, sbx run, teardown
'   internal/workspace/mount.go   — mount plan
'   packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh, defs/*/entrypoint.sh — in-container steps
' HISTORY: until 2026-10-16 the host flow also ran internal/egress (networks,
' sidecars, readiness, teardown), internal/broker (inject/strip) and
' internal/egressproxy (MITM + flows.ndjson). All three are DELETED with the
' docker+egress backend ("Retire Docker egress"; "Refuse without sbx").
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: defs/cursor/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh
'
' ── §2 · THE IMAGE READS NO .env; IT ONLY BRIDGES KEY ALIASES (N7, 2026-10-17) ─
' The user: "Keep 1+1, seed --env-file (Recommended)" (repo-simplification.puml
' N7). MEASURED: find_env_file is deleted, and load_env lost its sbx guard and
' its `set -a` sourcing of the workspace .env and is renamed bridge_google_keys
' (entrypoint-lib.sh:49-62); every def entrypoint calls bridge_google_keys, in
' the shell, BEFORE `proveo-entrypoint prep` (N1, 2026-10-17: prep keeps only the
' passwd entry, the git-context report and the smoke sentinel —
' _spec/cmd/proveo-entrypoint/prep-sequence.puml).
' internal/contract/env_prelude_test.go TestNeitherPreludeReadsTheWorkspaceEnv
' pins that neither the bash prelude nor prep reads it. The project .env's
' values now reach a NEW sandbox from the host, through sbx's own `--env-file`
' (_spec/internal/credentials/credential-decisions.puml, PROJECT .env).
' HISTORY: find_env_file tried ./.env, the git root (rev-parse, then a pure-bash
' walk), then any .env at `find -maxdepth 5`; load_env sourced it under `set -a`
' unless SANDBOX_NAME or SANDBOX_VM_ID was set (until 2026-10-16 the guard keyed
' on PROVEO_EGRESS_MODE).
'
' Provider key aliasing runs in both directions, because the ecosystem has not
' settled on one spelling: GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY is filled from
' GEMINI_API_KEY or GOOGLE_API_KEY when absent, and once it is set the two older
' names are filled back from it for tools that read only those. Every bridge
' fills an EMPTY slot and never overwrites, so a value the caller supplied wins.
' Bash is the only implementation since N1 deleted Go BridgeGoogleKeys
' (TestBashPreludeBridgesTheGoogleKeyAliases).
'
' HISTORY: apply_broker_sentinel rewrote every name in
' PROVEO_CREDENTIAL_BROKER_KEYS to PROVEO_BROKER_SENTINEL ("proveo-brokered") so
' proveo's MITM could inject on-route. It is DELETED with the MITM; on sbx the
' agent holds sbx's own placeholder (_spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml).
'
' ── §2c · WHY THE gh PROBE IS TIME-BOUNDED ────────────────────────────────
' report_git_context is read-only, but `gh auth status` validates GH_TOKEN and
' config sessions OVER THE NETWORK. Under a locked-down network policy that call
' can hang, and this runs before the agent, so it is capped at `timeout 5s` —
' an unanswered probe reports "not authenticated" rather than stalling startup.
' Seed never runs `gh auth login` and never installs gh: that is `proveo init`.
'
' The same reasoning caps the version banners: command_version_cecli and
' command_version_opencode both bound the call at 5s and fall back to a caller-
' supplied string. There are two spellings only because the harnesses pass their
' arguments in opposite orders (fallback-first vs command-first).
'
' _proveo_bounded is the one cap every such call goes through. Where `timeout`
' is missing (macOS, which the contract suite sources this lib on) it runs a
' bash 3.2 watchdog instead of running unbounded: `set -m` gives the command
' its own process group, and the watchdog signals the GROUP, as GNU timeout
' does — a server's grandchild `sleep` otherwise holds the pipe open and the
' caller's $(…) waits for it anyway. `<&0` is explicit because a background
' job's stdin is otherwise /dev/null; fd 3 keeps the command's stderr while
' the job-control notices go to /dev/null.
'
' ── §4 · A STEP THAT DEGRADES RATHER THAN FAILS ───────────────────────────
' attach_rtk (opt-in clone of rtk-ai/rtk into the workspace) was removed
' 2026-10-16 (Executor: "Remove rtk from proveo run"); _spec/_plans/repo-simplification.puml.
'
' run_smoke_test, under PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST=1, prints
' "PROVEO_SMOKE_READY <PROVEO_SMOKE_TARGET|target>" and then
' `exec sleep infinity` — the container stays up for inspection and the agent
' never starts. Anything a def prints AFTER its own run_smoke_test call is
' therefore unreachable in smoke mode
' (_spec/cmd/proveo-entrypoint/prep-process-boundary.puml).
'
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ConditionEndStyle hline

title proveo run <target> — sandbox lifecycle\n(host resolves → sbx sandbox runs the agent → host tears down)

start

partition "0 · Refuse unless sbx can run it  «host»" {
  :requireSandbox — sbx not ready\n→ refuse with the reason (no fallback; no manifest ""docker:"" key since F10);
}

partition "1 · LLM provider auth  «host»" {
  :detect provider from host env + project **.env**\n(filtered by the manifest's ""providers:"");
  if (declared key missing and a TTY?) then (prompt)
    :missing-env wizard — read secret (echo off),\nfeed provider detection;
  else (present)
  endif
  if (""--credentials forward""?) then (forward)
    :bare ""-e NAME"" — sbx copies the value\nfrom proveo's child env into the agent;
  else (broker — the default)
    :""sbx secret set --force"" (value on stdin)\nsbx's proxy attaches it at egress;
    note right
      Raw key never enters the agent.
      HISTORY: until 2026-10-16 the docker
      path wrote ""broker.env"" for proveo's
      MITM; both are deleted.
    end note
  endif
  :""WarnMountedSecrets"" — a workspace .env holding a\nprovider key is readable by the agent;
}

partition "2 · Filesystem mount  «host»" {
  :resolve git repo root + monorepo scope\n(interactive picker on a TTY);
  if (manifest ""workspace.layout""?) then (app — coding agents)
    :mount repo/scope **RW** at /app — agent EDITS IN PLACE\n(.git RW or RO per ""gitMode""; cursor/opencode=rw, cecli=ro);
    :monorepo subdir: hoist shared root files **RO**\n(package.json, CLAUDE.md, lockfiles …) · optional **RW** /app/output;
    note right
      **Coding-harness convention:** every coding
      harness mounts the repo **RW** at /app and
      keeps **.git RW** so the agent can edit code AND commit.
      Only analysis layouts opt out (""gitMode: ro"");
    end note
  else (app — analysis)
    :mount repo at /app (rw default; mode:ro optional)\n+ **RW** /app/output for artifacts (claudecode);
  endif
  :directory workspaces only — the plan binds no .env file\n(the /dev/null masks and /app/.env binds are deleted, F9);
  :project .env values → ""<run>/sbx/env"" → ""--env-file""\nat ""sbx create"" / ""sbx run"" of a NEW sandbox only (N7);
}

partition "3 · Egress  «host + sbx»" {
  :sbx's own policy decides egress (global baseline + ""sbx policy"");\nproveo reports it and never sets it;
  :Kit ""network.allow"" = add-on ports (host Ollama · CDP · adb)\n∪ own-agent credential domains — no tier entries;
  :ensure the agent image (""Deps.PreflightImages"", agent image only) —\nonly off ""--print"" and when sbx holds no template for it;
  note right
    HISTORY: until 2026-10-16 this step
    built docker networks, a Squid and a
    MITM sidecar per tier. All deleted.
  end note
}

partition "4 · Install defaults / dynamic  «agent: sbx startup / entrypoint.sh»" {
  :in-shell prelude FIRST (N1): workdir · ""bridge_google_keys""\n· ""bridge_git_identity"" — no .env load (N7);
  :""proveo-entrypoint prep"": run-as uid passwd entry (root-free)\n· git-context report · ""gh"" auth check · smoke sentinel;
  :seed BAKED defaults into ~/.<tool>\n(agents, config, hooks — image-immutable, offline);
  :tool setup via **jq** — cursor HTTP/1.1 fallback;
  :**code intelligence** — shared LSP detector\n(entrypoint-lib.sh §8: bash+awk) ranks workspace\nlanguages vs INSTALLED servers, ""command -v""-gated;
  if (agent has native LSP config?) then (yes)
    :render detector output to the agent's config (jq) —\nopencode.json ""lsp"" (opencode) ·\nplugin ""/.lsp.json"" (claudecode);
  else (MCP-capable, no native LSP)
    :wrap the detected servers in an MCP LSP bridge —\ncursor: **mcp-language-server** (Go, one/​server) → ~/.cursor/mcp.json ·\ncecli: **Serena** MCP toolkit → ""mcp-servers""\n(declared only when ""initialize"" answers);
  endif
  note right
    Servers are BAKED into the image, not
    downloaded at runtime: Node LSPs via the
    shared **base-node-lsp** layer (opencode,
    claudecode); **gopls** + **mcp-language-server**
    as static Go binaries (cursor); **Serena**
    via the existing Python venv (cecli).
  end note
  note left
    **This step is on the startup path, so its cost is
    the agent's time-to-first-prompt.** Two things kept
    it from being: a subshell per file, and a prune list
    that missed the package stores.

    ""_lsp_walk"" consults an extension map and a marker
    map for every file it sees. Read back through
    ""$(...)"" that is a fork each — and on a pnpm
    monorepo (123k files with ""node_modules"" already
    pruned) it made detection take ~85s on a tree
    ""find"" crosses in 3. The maps answer in ""REPLY""
    instead; every branch must set it, default
    included, or a no-match reports the previous
    file's language.

    ""\.pnpm-store"" alone was 110k of those 123k files,
    none of them ever a match: store objects are
    content-addressed and carry no extension. The prune
    expression now mirrors ""wsscan.AlwaysPrune"" so the
    host's tooling preview and this detector describe
    the same notion of workspace source.

    Ordering matters too. The step ran AFTER
    claudecode's ""Launching Claude Code..."" line, so its
    time read as the agent failing to start rather than
    prep still running. The launch line is now last
    before the ""exec"": whatever appears next is the
    agent's own output.
  end note
  :apply declarative env-var bridges (model routing);
  :DYNAMIC project tools when detected —\nmise / turbo / nx (fetched as sbx's policy allows);
  :exec agent CLI\n(agent installs the repo's own deps on demand);
  note left
  **Three contracts the shared lib holds for every entrypoint.**

  //No image sources the workspace "".env"" (N7, 2026-10-17).// A copy in the
  mounted tree must not be able to re-export keys into the agent process, so
  the lib no longer reads it at all; its values reach a new sandbox from the
  host through ""--env-file"", provider keys dropped unless forwarding.
  Non-secret harness flags travel in the Kit environment.

  //Agent evidence defaults to verbose.// The host ships
  ""PROVEO_AGENT_EVIDENCE"" and anything other than an explicit ""default""
  resolves to verbose, because a run nobody can read cannot be reviewed.
  Only the level is shared: each harness spells verbosity differently — and
  some only in headless mode — so every entrypoint builds its own flag list
  and reports what the level bought.

  //The detector has one output contract.// ""_lsp_walk"" emits
  one tab-separated lang + ftype pair per file, where ftype is the extension, or the filename
  for Docker, or empty when untracked; a marker file (""package\.json"",
  ""go\.mod"") is credited to its marker language AND to its own extension's
  language. Each harness renders that same stream into its own config —
  claudecode into a skills-directory plugin at
  ""~/\.claude/skills/proveo-lsp/\.lsp\.json"", which auto-loads on the next
  session with no marketplace involved.
  end note
}

partition "5 · Reports / logging, post-session  «host»" {
  :teardown saves ""sbx policy log"" to <egDir>/sbx/policy-log.json\n(allowed/blocked hosts — no MITM, so no flow record);
  :agent writes artifacts into reports/ (RW mount);
  :on exit OR SIGTERM/SIGHUP — **Teardown**: clone carry-back,\nstate save, ""sbx rm"" per the keep/remove decision;
}

stop


@enduml
